  "note": "Hand-entered, rounded figures from the original Orbis stories. Each series holds one year only. pop (2025): Circle after Danny Quah (2015), refining a 2013 observation by Reddit user valeriepieris: radius ≈ 3,300 km, centred near Mong Khet, Myanmar. Population figures ≈ 2025, UN World Population Prospects 2024, rounded. median_age (2024): Median ages ≈ 2024 and projections from UN World Population Prospects 2024 (medium scenario), rounded. Projections are scenarios, not certainties. electricity_access (2022): Access to electricity, % of population, ≈ 2022, World Bank / Tracking SDG7. Values rounded; countries not coloured are at or near universal access (≈ 95%+). cobalt_share (2023), lithium_share (2023), rare_earth_share (2023): Mine production shares ≈ 2023, US Geological Survey Mineral Commodity Summaries 2024, rounded. Refining shares ≈ IEA Global Critical Minerals Outlook 2024. China export controls: gallium and germanium (2023), graphite (2023), selected rare earths (2025). remit_usd (2023), remit_gdp (2023): World Bank Migration and Development Brief 40 (2024): ≈ USD 656 billion to low- and middle-income countries in 2023, larger than FDI and official aid combined (excl. China). Shares of GDP ≈ 2023, rounded. Flows drawn are major corridors, schematic. languages (2024): Ethnologue (2024): ≈ 7,160 living languages, ≈ 44% endangered; half the world speaks one of ≈ 23 languages. Language counts per country approximate.",
